COMMAND bash {run-worktree}/tests/fm-handoff-trigger.test.sh
ok - a firing rejects stale, dead, request-only and unacknowledged live successor records
ok - a second mate's handoff escalates to its parent once and its stop is never successor-gated (133, 116)
ok - default threshold: silent at 16% left, fires at 15% left before auto-compact
ok - threshold is configurable, 0 turns it off, and an unusable value keeps the default
ok - fires once per cycle across tool calls and prompts, and again for a new session
ok - a compaction re-arms the trigger for one more firing, and stale usage cannot spend it
ok - eight concurrent hook calls for one session fire exactly once
ok - compact point derives from Claude's autoCompactWindow layers and override, and a pin wins
ok - the settings layers resolve the way Claude resolves them, on canonical model names
ok - only integers from 100000 to 1000000 count as a settings window
ok - CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW overrides settings the way Claude reads it
ok - an unresolvable compact point or unreadable usage stays silent rather than guessing
ok - inert in a crew worktree, for Cursor payloads, other events, and a home without state; live in the primary
ok - a firing names every open captain order, and the stop is gated until the handoff lists them
ok - a recorded handoff gates the stop even with the trigger off, and an ordinary stop is never gated
ok - a handoff record gates only the session that wrote it, never another session's stop in the same home
ok - a caller outside any harness reads the captain's handoff, and a second harness session does not
